  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Flyer on the Driveway at Night",
    "overview": "The page is J&J's own black-and-gold job flyer turned into a physical object: a stack of heavy uppercase slabs set on a slate-night ground, lit by one color, the logo gold. The material of the trade is the ornament. Section breaks are the bottom hem of a corrugated roll-up door (steel slats, a gold weather strip, a dark rubber seal, a center handle notch), the work photo is revealed by that same door rolling up, and the hero is a canvas garage door the visitor lifts with a finger, spilling warm light onto the driveway.\n\nDensity is phone-first and generous with touch: every interactive target clears 44px, primary actions are 56px tall, lists are full-bleed ruled rows rather than cards. Type does the heavy lifting; there are no illustrations beyond the door itself, no stock imagery, no icon cards. The page is bilingual English/Spanish, with both languages present in the markup and one shown at a time, so every component must hold either language's length.\n\nThe system font stack is a deliberate house rule set by the site's builder (Ellie) for pitch sites, not an oversight. The flyer voice comes from weight (900), caps, and tight negative tracking, never from a loaded face.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Slate-night ground, never pure black; warm-white ink; logo gold as the only accent fill.",
      "Heavy system caps (900, uppercase, negative tracking, line-height under 1) stacked like flyer type.",
      "Roll-up door material (corrugated slats + gold hem) as dividers and reveals.",
      "Full-bleed hairline-ruled lists instead of cards.",
      "Phone-first single column; desktop adapts at 1024px into two-column splits.",
      "Bilingual EN/ES throughout, toggled at the document root."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Gold Rule",
        "body": "Gold is the only accent fill. Any new emphasis, state, or badge uses gold or nothing; no second warm or saturated hue enters the page.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Never-Black Rule",
        "body": "The darkest page surface is slate night (`ground`). Pure #000 is not a surface color; near-black values appear only inside the door material (seals, handle notch, lanterns).",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Slate-on-Gold Rule",
        "body": "Text and icons on a gold fill are always `on-gold` slate.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
